#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092019 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "3e096041-22f8-5b7e-88d7-eca10203a379" :question/math-academy-id "e-5470" :question/problem "Consider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with the standard matrix $T$, given below?\n$\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/989/Source/Images/db07fd70ec06ccd7ac9258c2f4c75f22.png)" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$, we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $\\mathbf{T}(D)$ under the action of $\\mathbf{T}$:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(\\mathbf{T}(D)) = \\mid \\det(T) \\mid \\cdot \\text{Area}(D)\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D) = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 = 6\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T$, we get\n\n$$\n\\det(T) = 4 \\cdot 2 - 2 \\cdot (-1) = 10\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nArea(T(D)) &= \\begin{vmatrix}det(T) & \\cdot Area(D) \\\\ = & 10\\end{vmatrix}\\cdot 6 \\\\\n&= 60\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092020 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/id #uuid "e0f036c5-c27d-5a0e-aeb1-cb7c99b49691" :question/math-academy-id "e-5471" :question/problem "A triangle $D$ has vertices $(1,1)$, $(4,5)$, and $(-2,1)$. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with the standard matrix $T$, given below?\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/989/Source/Images/6c06e31f3407ba3e54c61c5b222b6d9d.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$, we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $\\mathbf{T}(D)$ under the action of $\\mathbf{T}$:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(\\mathbf{T}(D)) = \\mid \\det(T) \\mid \\cdot \\text{Area}(D)\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D) = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 = 6\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T$, we get\n\n$$\n\\det(T) = (-7) \\cdot 3 - 5 \\cdot (-2) = -11\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nArea(T(D)) &= \\begin{vmatrix}det(T) & \\cdot Area(D) \\\\ = & -11\\end{vmatrix}\\cdot 6 \\\\\n&= 66\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092074 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80a4eee7-a763-5c28-ae3c-5bce78222c87" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Area Scale Factor of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/id #uuid "53c7a748-dadb-516e-879b-92cd0c986041" :question/math-academy-id "e-7454" :question/problem "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ that is given by its standard matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $\\mid \\det(T) \\mid$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}det(T) & &= & 2 \\cdot 4 - 3 \\cdot 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\mid 8 - 3 \\mid \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092848 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96149e37-5e82-5ccb-9334-b811807c3195" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091554} {:answer/id #uuid "bffefaae-bcc4-56dd-b974-8199951f7843" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091555} {:answer/id #uuid "e76111a3-467c-5978-ad77-2e6023f788e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091556} {:answer/id #uuid "f6693318-6d61-5139-a7d1-fdc3c1a26af6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091557} {:answer/id #uuid "015e56af-bc5e-5c49-99a0-14854b238efc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "160" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091558}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6693318-6d61-5139-a7d1-fdc3c1a26af6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091557} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a3f1cd4-20ab-5644-81a4-94e41a1db6fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091553}] :question/id #uuid "45faf24d-552b-523b-9d7b-94bb05598c82" :question/math-academy-id "q-9302" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/989/Source/Images/q-9302.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T$, given below?\n$T = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$."}]}
